{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_23f5244459f5:reviewer:plan:plan:1","created_at":"2026-09-23 12:55:38","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"agent","role":"reviewer","provider":"claude-code"}},"payload":{"step_name":"reviewer:plan","phase":"plan","iteration":1,"result_json":{"readiness":"ready_with_corrections","items":[{"id":"P1.1","title":"Workspace header is wrong for resumed OpenCode sessions","action":"auto_fix","reason":"OpenCodeProvider.resumeSession ignores ResumeOptions.workingDirectory and uses the stored session.directory, so recording the requested workdir contradicts the Phase 2 gate (actual provider workspace on resume).","priority":"P1","scopeClass":"acceptance_required","effortDelta":1,"architectureDelta":0,"estimateConfidence":"medium","failure":"A resumed OpenCode session from a different workdir or worktree logs the wrong workspace, so all targets are shortened against the wrong root or mislabeled as outside the workspace.","lowestCostCorrection":"Record the session-reported effective workspace (optional AgentSession.workingDirectory set by OpenCodeSession from session.directory and by the CLI providers from their cwd); use the requested workdir only for fresh sessions; omit workspace when unknown on resume; add an OpenCode resume fixture whose directory differs from the request."},{"id":"P1.2","title":"TUI signal handling ignores existing cli-lifecycle signal owner","action":"auto_fix","reason":"bin.ts installs cli-lifecycle, which aborts getCliAbortSignal and force-exits via process.exit(130/143) after a 2s grace or a second signal; the plan adds separate handlers and never mentions it, so TUI cleanup in finally can be bypassed and SIGTERM does not reach the watcher.","priority":"P1","scopeClass":"acceptance_required","effortDelta":1,"architectureDelta":0,"estimateConfidence":"high","failure":"A double SIGINT/SIGTERM, or cleanup stalled past the grace window, exits the process with the terminal left in raw mode on the alternate screen, violating the requirement that exceptional exits restore the terminal.","lowestCostCorrection":"Merge getCliAbortSignal() into the controller abort, take the exit status from getCliAbortCause() (130/143), register a synchronous idempotent terminal restore on process exit while the UI is entered, and add PTY double-signal and grace-timeout cases."},{"id":"P1.3","title":"Bounded rotating drain reorders legacy raw/human replay across files","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The 256-record/256 KiB drain budget and source rotation are unconditional changes to the shared NdjsonTailer; today poll() drains each file completely in sorted order. The existing small-fixture tests would not catch the change.","priority":"P1","scopeClass":"acceptance_required","effortDelta":1,"architectureDelta":0,"estimateConfidence":"high","failure":"Replaying two invocation backlogs over 256 records in --human-readable mode interleaves them in 256-record chunks with repeated label headers, breaking the existing output contract that requirements section 7 says must be kept.","lowestCostCorrection":"Drain historical (pre-watermark) data in sorted file order to completion across turns; apply rotation only to live data or only under the TUI option; add a multi-file backlog of more than 256 records per file as a regression test for raw and human modes."},{"id":"P1.4","title":"Paused viewport snapshot of rendered rows cannot survive resize","action":"auto_fix","reason":"Design Decisions stores bounded rendered rows while paused, but W6/W7 require resize to recompute layout while keeping selection and inspection; rows rendered for one width cannot be re-wrapped for another.","priority":"P1","scopeClass":"acceptance_required","effortDelta":1,"architectureDelta":0,"estimateConfidence":"high","failure":"Resizing from 140x40 to 40x6 while paused either overflows or clips the snapshot, or discards it and loses operator focus, failing the resize-preserves-focus acceptance criterion.","lowestCostCorrection":"Snapshot bounded width-independent row models (stable IDs, sanitized text, inspector detail) under the existing 256 KiB cap and render them at the current size; add a pause-resize-restore controller test."},{"id":"P2.1","title":"Phase 1 compiled/subprocess smoke has no entry point","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The Phase 1 gate requires source and compiled evidence for the adapter, but --tui is not exposed until Phase 6 and bun run build compiles only src/bin.ts.","priority":"P2","scopeClass":"risk_reduction","effortDelta":0,"architectureDelta":0,"estimateConfidence":"high","failure":"The Phase 1 compatibility gate cannot be checked as written, so renderer selection could be accepted without compiled-binary evidence.","lowestCostCorrection":"Name a test-only fixture entry (for example test/fixtures/watch-terminal-smoke.ts) and the exact bun build --compile command used to produce the recorded evidence."}],"summary":"Strong plan that covers requirements 208 and fixes the tailer's unbounded queue at the source. Four mechanical P1 corrections: resumed OpenCode workspace, integration with the cli-lifecycle signal owner, legacy replay ordering under bounded draining, and a resize-safe paused snapshot. One P2 gap in Phase 1 gate testability.","baselineAssessment":{"independentEffortEstimate":32,"confidence":"medium","reason":"W1/W3/W4/W5/W7 scores are plausible; W2 (public contract, three mappers incl. new Claude stream message/block tracking, workspace producer with resume correction) and W6 (controller, key surface, viewport model, CLI preflight, cli-lifecycle integration) are each about 2 points light."},"budget":{"B0":28,"B":28,"I":32,"W":28,"R":4,"projectedEffort":32,"S":35,"N":0,"D":0,"E":35,"A":42,"P":9,"baselineDirection":"aligned","budgetBand":"within_standard","budgetAlerts":["positive_architecture_exceeded"],"requiresHuman":true,"positiveArchitectureLimit":7,"baselineDisagreementThreshold":7,"thresholds":{"growthPercent":25,"minimumGrowthPoints":2,"debtTradeoffRatio":1,"maxDebtCreditPercent":25,"absoluteGrowthPercent":50,"baselineDisagreementPercent":25,"minimumBaselineDisagreementPoints":2,"maxPositiveArchitecturePercent":25,"minimumPositiveArchitecturePoints":2,"singleArchitectureReviewPoints":5}},"governance":{"reviewKind":"initial","normalizedReadiness":"ready_with_corrections","route":"author_revision","gateCauses":[{"kind":"budget_alert","alert":"positive_architecture_exceeded","itemIds":[],"workItemIds":[]}],"findingOutcomes":[],"diagnostics":[],"hypotheticalEnforcedRoute":"human_gate"}},"head_commit":"95817c31f4b5c665346e0171edf2ea155222d30d","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":216007,"tokens_in":54,"tokens_out":22802,"cost_usd":1.7180303999999997,"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}
